      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/1/95/5462",
      "text": [
        " :\nسَأَلْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَنِ اَلرَّجُلِ أَوْصَى بِمَالِهِ فِي سَبِيلِ اَللَّهِ فَقَالَ \"أَعْطِهِ لِمَنْ أَوْصَى لَهُ بِهِ وَ إِنْ كَانَ يَهُودِيّاً أَوْ نَصْرَانِيّاً إِنَّ اَللَّهَ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ يَقُولُ\n۝ فَمَنْ بَدَّلَهُ بَعْدَ مٰا سَمِعَهُ فَإِنَّمٰا إِثْمُهُ عَلَى اَلَّذِينَ يُبَدِّلُونَهُ ۝."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5462 - Hammad ibn ʿIsa narrated from Hariz from Muhammad ibn Muslim, who said:\nI asked Abu Abdullah (as) about a man who made a will to give his wealth in the way of Allah (swt).\nImam (as) replied: \"Give it to the one he specified in his will, even if that person is a Jew or a Christian. Indeed, Allah (swt), the Almighty and Majestic, says:\n'But whoever changes it after hearing it, the sin is only upon those who change it.'\"\n(Surah Al-Baqarah 2:181)"
        ]
      }
    },
